-- Ministry of Personnel, Public Grievances and Pensions (Department of
-- Personnel and Training; Department of Pension and Pensioners' Welfare
-- — the latter issues the CCS (Pension)/NPS-gratuity items below under
-- the same ministry). Deepened 2026-09-04 (depth pass — see
-- docs/DEPTH_PASS_PLAN.md) beyond the original bounded pass (3 pairs).
-- Generated from the research log by a one-off script (scratchpad
-- gen_dopt.py); all 4 tracker listing pages (153 notifications) were
-- enumerated, 60 Full Texts read, two spot-checked verbatim against the
-- official egazette.gov.in PDF (CAT s.14(3) and s.18 chains).
--
-- The CCS (CCA) Rules chain gained a real intermediate: G.S.R. 337(E)'s
-- own Note says "last amended vide G.S.R. 18(E) dated the 10th January,
-- 2023" — inserted; nothing enumerates the 1965-2023 history. The
-- already-modeled G.S.R. 331(E) is now identified from its own text as
-- the IPS (Fixation of Cadre Strength) Sixth Amendment Regulations, 2025
-- (Telangana) and re-parented into that chain.
--
-- 23 further subject threads. Modeling choices, stated once:
--   - Enumerated Note lists are modeled as LINEAR chains (item[i] amends
--     item[i-1]) as everywhere else in this project, EXCEPT where the
--     citing preambles themselves say each amendment is made "in the
--     notification ... G.S.R. 730(E)" (CAT s.14(3), s.18) or the Note
--     says "subsequently amended by notification vide number" of a bare
--     principal (IAS/IPS/IFS Cadre Rules) — those are HUBS (each amends
--     the principal directly).
--   - Lists that interleave file-number-only items (IAS/IPS Appointment
--     by Promotion Regulations, whose principals are themselves
--     file-number-only) are modeled as chain SEGMENTS between consecutive
--     numbered items; no edge bridges an unmodelable item, and the
--     first numbered item after a gap has no incoming edge.
--   - Per-cadre (state) tables under the IAS/IPS (Fixation of Cadre
--     Strength) Regulations, 1955 are linear per state; omnibus
--     notifications that every state table repeats (e.g. 319(E)
--     1995-03-31, 739(E) 1997-12-31, 188(E) 2009-03-24) are ONE node
--     with branching edges, deduplicated by (number, date) within an
--     instrument only — never across instruments.
--   - Two-column tables print "213E"/"320E"; normalized to "(E)".
--
-- REAL DRAFTING INCONSISTENCIES kept as observed, not reconciled: the
-- IPS (Pay) Rules have two lineages that never cite each other (the
-- rule-5 amendments 915(E)/874(E) vs the 36-row state-schedule table);
-- the IAS/IPS Appointment-by-Promotion twin lists disagree on several
-- shared dates (G.S.R. 118 "15-03-1958" vs "28-02-1958"); IPS Haryana and
-- Bihar cadre tables are the identical list for 1974-2010 (copy-paste
-- lineage); G.S.R. 636(E)'s preamble names the wrong principal year.
-- Deferred rather than guessed: the CCS (Pension) Rules' October 2022
-- amendment is cited as "G.S.R. 770(E)" by one DoPPW Note and
-- "G.S.R. 710(E)" by another — not modeled; G.S.R. 635(E) (Tripura IAS
-- cadre) carries a Note listing the WEST BENGAL cadre's amendments —
-- table skipped, 635(E) modeled as amending the principal directly;
-- the IFS cadre-strength 157-row table was not transcribed inline.
--
-- Cross-cadre pattern worth knowing: DoPT issues every AIS state
-- notification as a cadre-strength (AIS-II(A)) / pay (AIS-II(B)) twin
-- with consecutive numbers on the same date, and corrects them in twins.
--
-- Collisions within this ministry kept distinct by year (and by month-day
-- where the same number recurs in one year): 331(E) 2024/2025, 472(E)
-- 2025/2026, 471(E) 2024/2026, 687(E) 2024/2025, 445(E) 2024/2025 (both
-- in the IAS Pay table), 862/863(E) 2016/2023, 102(E) 1985/2024, 21(E)
-- 2000/2026, 750(E) 1976/2023, and many more inside the tables.
--
-- Real leads NOT modeled: IFS (Probationers' Final Examination)
-- Regulations, 2016 and CBI (Senior Police Posts) RR 2013 supersessions
-- (title only); Civil Services Examination Rules corrigenda (Part I,
-- target by date only); a CBI DSP LDCE corrigendum "of even number";
-- G.S.R. 773(E) whose target number appears only in the target's own
-- text; principals cited only by file number (Appointment by Promotion
-- 1955, IAS Probationers' Final Examination 1955, AIS Joint Cadre 1972).


